IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, part sfad: Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (4), Exemptions: s 272 (no consideration), s 272A (small offers), s 272B (private placement)
-- (lines 42644-43380 of SFA2001.txt). Imports prelude, daydate, sfa-core and sfa-periods (every period is counted by sfa-periods, never here).
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   Each of ss 272, 272A and 272B says that "Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257) do not apply" to an offer
--   "if" its conditions are met. The function for the section answers JUST TRUE when every condition is met, JUST FALSE when a condition the text
--   states with "if" is not met (the "In short" sentence of the Guide, and a marginal reading for a lawyer: "if A then B" does not itself say
--   "if not A then not B"), and NOTHING where the offer is outside what the section speaks of, or a condition's answer is not known.
--   Every limb of a section is its own function; the function for the section takes the limbs' answers as inputs of type MAYBE BOOLEAN, the way the keel does.
--   Amounts, numbers and factors the Act leaves to the Authority (another amount, another number of persons, the factors of a "closely related offer") are inputs.
--   "-- FORK" lines are collected into the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `s 272: issue or transfer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts for no consideration`

-- src:42649 | 272.—(1) Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other
-- src:42650 | than section 257) do not apply to an offer of securities being shares or
-- src:42651 | debentures of an entity, or units in a business trust, if no consideration
-- src:42652 | is or will be given for the issue or transfer of the shares or debentures,
-- src:42653 | or units in a business trust (as the case may be).
@ref s 272(1) (src:42649-42653)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of securities being shares or debentures of an entity, or units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities that are shares or debentures of an entity, or units in a business trust?
    `consideration is or will be given for the issue or transfer of the shares or debentures, or units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is, or will, any consideration be given for the issue or transfer of the shares or debentures, or units in a business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offer is an offer of securities being shares or debentures of an entity, or units in a business trust`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offer of securities being shares or debentures of an entity, or units in a business trust"
        IF `consideration is or will be given for the issue or transfer of the shares or debentures, or units in a business trust`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if no consideration is or will be given for the issue or transfer of the shares or debentures"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- FORK s272-1 | s 272(1) | `s 272(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` | took JUST FALSE where consideration is or will be given (a condition introduced with "if") and NOTHING where the offer is not an offer of shares, debentures or business-trust units (the section speaks only of those) | other reading NOTHING for the first (an "if" condition does not itself say "if not then not") and JUST FALSE for the second | licence {IN-SHORT} for the first and {P-c} for the second; the first is also under "Marginal readings for a lawyer"

-- src:42659 | (2) Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than
-- src:42660 | section 257) do not apply to an offer of securities‑based derivatives
-- src:42661 | contracts being units of shares or debentures of an entity, or
-- src:42662 | derivatives of units in a business trust, if —
-- src:42664 | (a) no consideration is or will be given for the issue or transfer
-- src:42665 | of the units of shares or debentures of the entity, or
-- src:42666 | derivatives of units in the business trust; and
-- src:42668 | (b) no consideration is or will be given for the underlying
-- src:42669 | shares or debentures of the entity, or units in the business
-- src:42670 | trust (as the case may be) on the exercise or conversion of
-- src:42671 | the units of shares or debentures of the entity, or derivatives
-- src:42672 | of units in the business trust (as the case may be).
@ref s 272(2) (src:42659-42672)
GIVEN
    `the offer is an offer of securities-based derivatives contracts being units of shares or debentures of an entity, or derivatives of units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities-based derivatives contracts that are units of shares or debentures of an entity, or derivatives of units in a business trust?
    `consideration is or will be given for the issue or transfer of the units of shares or debentures of the entity, or derivatives of units in the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is, or will, any consideration be given for the issue or transfer of the units of shares or debentures of the entity, or derivatives of units in the business trust?
    `consideration is or will be given for the underlying shares or debentures of the entity, or units in the business trust, on the exercise or conversion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is, or will, any consideration be given for the underlying shares or debentures of the entity, or units in the business trust, on the exercise or conversion of the units or derivatives?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272(2) the offer of securities-based derivatives contracts is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offer is an offer of securities-based derivatives contracts being units of shares or debentures of an entity, or derivatives of units in a business trust`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offer of securities-based derivatives contracts being units of shares or debentures of an entity, or derivatives of units in a business trust"
        IF `consideration is or will be given for the issue or transfer of the units of shares or debentures of the entity, or derivatives of units in the business trust`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no consideration is or will be given for the issue or transfer of the units of shares or debentures of the entity"
        IF `consideration is or will be given for the underlying shares or debentures of the entity, or units in the business trust, on the exercise or conversion`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no consideration is or will be given for the underlying shares or debentures of the entity, or units in the business trust"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- FORK s272-2 | s 272(2) | `s 272(2) the offer of securities-based derivatives contracts is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` | took JUST FALSE where either paragraph (a) or paragraph (b) is not met (both are conditions of an "if" joined by "and") and NOTHING where the offer is not of the kind named | other reading NOTHING for the first | licence {IN-SHORT} and {P-c}; under "Marginal readings for a lawyer"

§ `s 272A: small offers (definitions the section uses)`

-- "advertisement" (s 272A(10)), the meaning of the affairs of the person making the offer (s 272A(11)) and the kinds of selling or promotional expense are used by
-- s 272A(1)(c), (1)(d), (8)(c)(iv), (8)(c)(v) and by s 272B(1)(b) and (1)(c) (s 272B(6) takes the meaning of "advertisement" from s 272A(10)).

-- src:43152 | (10) In subsections (1)(c) and (8)(c)(iv), “advertisement” means —
-- src:43154 | (a) a written or printed communication;
-- src:43156 | (b) a communication by radio, television or other medium of
-- src:43157 | communication; or
-- src:43159 | (c) a communication by means of a recorded telephone
-- src:43160 | message,
-- src:43162 | that is published in connection with an offer of securities or
-- src:43163 | securities‑based derivatives contracts, but does not include —
-- src:43168 | (d) a document —
-- src:43170 | (i) purporting to describe the securities or
-- src:43171 | securities‑based derivatives contracts being offered,
-- src:43172 | or the business and affairs of the person making the
-- src:43173 | offer, the issuer or (where applicable) the underlying
-- src:43174 | entity, or (where the securities or securities‑based
-- src:43175 | derivatives contracts being offered are units or
-- src:43176 | derivatives of units in a business trust) the business
-- src:43177 | trust; and
-- src:43179 | (ii) purporting to have been prepared for delivery to and
-- src:43180 | review by persons to whom the offer is made so as to
-- src:43181 | assist them in making an investment decision in
-- src:43182 | respect of the securities or securities‑based
-- src:43183 | derivatives contracts being offered;
-- src:43185 | (e) a publication which consists solely of a disclosure, notice
-- src:43186 | or report required under this Act, or any listing rules or
-- src:43187 | other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas
-- src:43188 | exchange, which is made by any person; or
-- src:43190 | (f) a publication which consists solely of a notice or report of a
-- src:43191 | general meeting or proposed general meeting of the person
-- src:43192 | making the offer, the issuer, the unitholders of the business
-- src:43193 | trust, the underlying entity or any entity, or a presentation
-- src:43194 | of oral or written material on matters so contained in the
-- src:43195 | notice or report at the general meeting.
@ref s 272A(10) (src:43152-43195)
GIVEN
    `the communication is a written or printed communication, a communication by radio, television or other medium of communication, or a communication by means of a recorded telephone message` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication a written or printed communication, a communication by radio, television or other medium of communication, or a communication by means of a recorded telephone message?
    `the communication is published in connection with an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication published in connection with an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the communication is a document purporting to describe the securities or the business and affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the business trust, and purporting to have been prepared for delivery to and review by persons to whom the offer is made so as to assist them in making an investment decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication a document that purports to describe the securities or contracts being offered, or the business and affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the business trust, and purports to have been prepared for delivery to and review by the persons to whom the offer is made so as to assist them in making an investment decision?
    `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under this Act, or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication a publication that consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under the Securities and Futures Act 2001, or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange?
    `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting, or a presentation of material on matters so contained at the general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication a publication that consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting of the person making the offer, the issuer, the unitholders of the business trust, the underlying entity or any entity, or a presentation of oral or written material on matters so contained in the notice or report at the general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(10) the communication is an advertisement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the communication is a written or printed communication, a communication by radio, television or other medium of communication, or a communication by means of a recorded telephone message` AND `the communication is published in connection with an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“advertisement” means — (a) a written or printed communication; (b) a communication by radio, television or other medium of communication; or (c) a communication by means of a recorded telephone message, that is published in connection with an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts"
        IF `the communication is a document purporting to describe the securities or the business and affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the business trust, and purporting to have been prepared for delivery to and review by persons to whom the offer is made so as to assist them in making an investment decision` OR `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under this Act, or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange` OR `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting, or a presentation of material on matters so contained at the general meeting`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    -- FORK s272A-10 | s 272A(10) | `s 272A(10) the communication is an advertisement` | took the definition as closed ("means"), so a communication outside paragraphs (a) to (c) is JUST FALSE, and one inside an exclusion (d), (e) or (f) is JUST FALSE | other reading none: "means" closes the term (the delegated-definitions ruling distinguishes a bare list; this is a definition that says "means") | licence {IN-SHORT} ("a means definition"). Paragraph (d) is read as both of its sub-paragraphs (i) and (ii) joined by "and", given as one input.

-- src:43199 | (11) In subsection (10)(d)(i), the reference to the affairs of the
-- src:43200 | person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the
-- src:43201 | business trust includes —
-- src:43203 | (a) in the case where the person making the offer, the issuer or
-- src:43204 | the underlying entity is a corporation, a reference to the
-- src:43205 | matters mentioned in section 2(2);
-- src:43207 | (b) in any other case, a reference to such matters as may be
-- src:43208 | prescribed by regulations made under section 341.
@ref s 272A(11) (src:43199-43208)
GIVEN
    `the person making the offer, the issuer or the underlying entity is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the offer, the issuer or the underlying entity a corporation?
    `the matter is within section 2(2) as the keel answers it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 2(2) the matter is within the affairs of a corporation` answer for the matter? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the matter is one prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one that the Authority has prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(11) the matter is included in the affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the business trust` MEANS
    IF `the person making the offer, the issuer or the underlying entity is a corporation`
    THEN `the matter is within section 2(2) as the keel answers it`
    ELSE IF `the matter is one prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such matters as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341"
    -- FORK s272A-11 | s 272A(11) | `s 272A(11) the matter is included in the affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the business trust` | took "includes" as an extension, so a matter that is neither within section 2(2) nor prescribed answers NOTHING, never JUST FALSE | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {IN-SHORT} ("says includes" answers NOTHING)

DECLARE `s 272A(1)(d) kind of selling or promotional expense` IS ONE OF
    `s 272A(1)(d) an expense incurred for administrative or professional services`
    `s 272A(1)(d)(i) a commission or fee for services rendered by the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
    `s 272A(1)(d)(ii) a commission or fee for services rendered by an exempt person in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
    `s 272A(1)(d)(iii)(A) a commission or fee for services rendered by a person licensed, approved, authorised or otherwise regulated under the laws of a foreign jurisdiction in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
    `s 272A(1)(d)(iii)(B) a commission or fee for services rendered by a person exempted from those foreign laws, codes or requirements in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
    `s 272A(1)(d) any other selling or promotional expense`

-- src:42754 | (d) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred in
-- src:42755 | connection with each offer other than those incurred for
-- src:42756 | administrative or professional services, or by way of
-- src:42757 | commission or fee for services rendered by —
-- src:42759 | (i) the holder of a capital markets services licence to
-- src:42760 | deal in capital markets products that are securities or
-- src:42761 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:42763 | (ii) an exempt person in respect of dealing in capital
-- src:42764 | markets products that are securities or
-- src:42765 | securities‑based derivatives contracts; or
-- src:42767 | (iii) a person —
-- src:42769 | (A) who is licensed, approved, authorised or
-- src:42770 | otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or
-- src:42771 | other requirements of any foreign jurisdiction
-- src:42772 | in respect of dealing in capital markets
-- src:42777 | products that are securities or securities‑based
-- src:42778 | derivatives contracts; or
-- src:42780 | (B) who is exempted from the laws, codes or
-- src:42781 | requirements mentioned in sub‑paragraph (A)
-- src:42782 | in respect of dealing in capital markets
-- src:42783 | products that are securities or securities‑based
-- src:42784 | derivatives contracts; and
@ref s 272A(1)(d) (src:42754-42784)
GIVEN
    `the kind of the selling or promotional expense` IS A `s 272A(1)(d) kind of selling or promotional expense` @desc Which kind is the selling or promotional expense paid or incurred in connection with the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(1)(d) the expense is one the exemption allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of the selling or promotional expense`
    WHEN `s 272A(1)(d) an expense incurred for administrative or professional services` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 272A(1)(d)(i) a commission or fee for services rendered by the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 272A(1)(d)(ii) a commission or fee for services rendered by an exempt person in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 272A(1)(d)(iii)(A) a commission or fee for services rendered by a person licensed, approved, authorised or otherwise regulated under the laws of a foreign jurisdiction in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 272A(1)(d)(iii)(B) a commission or fee for services rendered by a person exempted from those foreign laws, codes or requirements in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 272A(1)(d) any other selling or promotional expense` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred in connection with each offer other than those incurred for administrative or professional services"

-- The same list is used by s 272A(8)(c)(v) and s 272B(1)(c): each section's own list function below reads every expense through this one.
@ref s 272A(1)(d) (src:42754-42784)
GIVEN
    `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with each offer` IS A LIST OF `s 272A(1)(d) kind of selling or promotional expense` @desc What are the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with each offer? (An empty list: none are paid or incurred.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(1)(d) the selling or promotional expenses are ones the exemption allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with each offer`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN k FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `s 272A(1)(d) the expense is one the exemption allows` k EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN `s 272A(1)(d) the selling or promotional expenses are ones the exemption allows` rest
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred in connection with each offer other than those incurred for administrative or professional services, or by way of commission or fee for services rendered by"
    -- FORK s272A-1d | s 272A(1)(d) | `s 272A(1)(d) the selling or promotional expenses are ones the exemption allows` | took the expenses one by one: every expense must be an administrative or professional one, or a commission or fee for services rendered by a person named in (i), (ii) or (iii) | other reading the persons named qualify all expenses of a total, not each | licence the text's own "no ... expenses ... other than those"

-- src:42750 | (c) none of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement
-- src:42751 | making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended
-- src:42752 | offer;
@ref s 272A(1)(c) (src:42750-42752)
GIVEN
    `one of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any of the offers accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(1)(c) none of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement` MEANS
    IF `one of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "none of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `s 272A: small offers (the personal offer and the limbs of subsection (1))`

-- src:42813 | (a) may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made;
-- src:42814 | and
@ref s 272A(3)(a) (src:42813-42814)
GIVEN
    `the offer may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the offer be accepted only by the person to whom it is made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(3)(a) the offer may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made` MEANS
    IF `the offer may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a personal offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts is one that — (a) may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made"

-- src:42854 | (F) a person —
-- src:42856 | (FA) who is licensed, approved, authorised
-- src:42857 | or otherwise regulated under the laws,
-- src:42858 | codes or other requirements of any
-- src:42859 | foreign jurisdiction in respect of
-- src:42860 | dealing in capital markets products
-- src:42861 | that are securities or securities‑based
-- src:42862 | derivatives contracts;
-- src:42864 | (FB) who is exempted from the laws, codes
-- src:42865 | or requirements mentioned in
-- src:42866 | sub‑paragraph (FA) in respect of
-- src:42867 | dealing in capital markets products
-- src:42872 | that are securities or securities‑based
-- src:42873 | derivatives contracts;
-- src:42875 | (FC) who is licensed, approved, authorised
-- src:42876 | or otherwise regulated under the laws,
-- src:42877 | codes or other requirements of any
-- src:42878 | foreign jurisdiction in respect of the
-- src:42879 | provision of financial advisory services
-- src:42880 | concerning investment products; or
-- src:42882 | (FD) who is exempted from the laws, codes
-- src:42883 | or requirements mentioned in
-- src:42884 | sub‑paragraph (FC) in respect of the
-- src:42885 | provision of financial advisory services
-- src:42886 | concerning investment products.
@ref s 272A(3)(b)(iii)(F) (src:42854-42886)
GIVEN
    `the person to whom the indication was made is licensed, approved, authorised or otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or other requirements of a foreign jurisdiction in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the indication was made licensed, approved, authorised or otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or other requirements of any foreign jurisdiction in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the person to whom the indication was made is exempted from the laws, codes or requirements mentioned in sub-paragraph (FA) in respect of dealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the indication was made exempted from those foreign laws, codes or requirements in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the person to whom the indication was made is licensed, approved, authorised or otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or other requirements of a foreign jurisdiction in respect of the provision of financial advisory services concerning investment products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the indication was made licensed, approved, authorised or otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or other requirements of any foreign jurisdiction in respect of the provision of financial advisory services concerning investment products?
    `the person to whom the indication was made is exempted from the laws, codes or requirements mentioned in sub-paragraph (FC) in respect of the provision of financial advisory services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the indication was made exempted from those foreign laws, codes or requirements in respect of the provision of financial advisory services concerning investment products?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(3)(b)(iii)(F) the person to whom the indication was made is a foreign regulated or exempt person` MEANS
    IF `the person to whom the indication was made is licensed, approved, authorised or otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or other requirements of a foreign jurisdiction in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` OR `the person to whom the indication was made is exempted from the laws, codes or requirements mentioned in sub-paragraph (FA) in respect of dealing` OR `the person to whom the indication was made is licensed, approved, authorised or otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or other requirements of a foreign jurisdiction in respect of the provision of financial advisory services concerning investment products` OR `the person to whom the indication was made is exempted from the laws, codes or requirements mentioned in sub-paragraph (FC) in respect of the provision of financial advisory services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to any of the following persons"

-- src:42829 | (iii) any previous indication (whether through statements
-- src:42830 | made or actions carried out) before that date by that
-- src:42831 | person that indicate to any of the following persons
-- src:42832 | that that person is interested in offers of that kind:
-- src:42834 | (A) the person making the offer;
-- src:42836 | (B) the holder of a capital markets services licence
-- src:42837 | to deal in capital markets products that are
-- src:42838 | securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:42839 | contracts;
-- src:42841 | (C) an exempt person in respect of dealing in
-- src:42842 | capital markets products that are securities or
-- src:42843 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:42845 | (D) a person licensed under the Financial Advisers
-- src:42846 | Act 2001 in respect of the provision of
-- src:42847 | financial advisory services concerning
-- src:42848 | investment products;
-- src:42850 | (E) an exempt financial adviser as defined in
-- src:42851 | section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers
-- src:42852 | Act 2001;
@ref s 272A(3)(b)(iii) (src:42829-42852)
GIVEN
    `the person has previously indicated to the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person, by statements or actions before the date of the offer, indicate to the person making the offer that the person is interested in offers of that kind?
    `the person has previously indicated to the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person, by statements or actions before the date of the offer, indicate to the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts that the person is interested in offers of that kind?
    `the person has previously indicated to an exempt person in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person, by statements or actions before the date of the offer, indicate to an exempt person in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts that the person is interested in offers of that kind?
    `the person has previously indicated to a person licensed under the Financial Advisers Act 2001 in respect of the provision of financial advisory services concerning investment products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person, by statements or actions before the date of the offer, indicate to a person licensed under the Financial Advisers Act 2001 in respect of the provision of financial advisory services concerning investment products that the person is interested in offers of that kind?
    `the person has previously indicated to an exempt financial adviser as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person, by statements or actions before the date of the offer, indicate to an exempt financial adviser as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001 that the person is interested in offers of that kind?
    `the person has previously indicated to a person described in sub-paragraph (F)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(3)(b)(iii)(F) the person to whom the indication was made is a foreign regulated or exempt person` answer for the person to whom the indication was made? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(3)(b)(iii) the person has previously indicated that the person is interested in offers of that kind` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has previously indicated to the person making the offer` OR `the person has previously indicated to the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` OR `the person has previously indicated to an exempt person in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` OR `the person has previously indicated to a person licensed under the Financial Advisers Act 2001 in respect of the provision of financial advisory services concerning investment products` OR `the person has previously indicated to an exempt financial adviser as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001` OR (`the person has previously indicated to a person described in sub-paragraph (F)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person has previously indicated to a person described in sub-paragraph (F)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the indication was made to a person described in sub-paragraph (F) is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that indicate to any of the following persons that that person is interested in offers of that kind"

-- src:42816 | (b) is made to a person who is likely to be interested in that
-- src:42817 | offer, having regard to —
-- src:42819 | (i) any previous contact before the date of the offer
-- src:42820 | between the person making the offer and that person;
-- src:42825 | (ii) any previous professional or other connection
-- src:42826 | established before that date between the person
-- src:42827 | making the offer and that person; or
@ref s 272A(3)(b) (src:42816-42827)
GIVEN
    `the person is likely to be interested in that offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the offer is made likely to be interested in that offer?
    `there was previous contact before the date of the offer between the person making the offer and that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there any previous contact before the date of the offer between the person making the offer and that person?
    `there was a previous professional or other connection established before that date between the person making the offer and that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there any previous professional or other connection established before the date of the offer between the person making the offer and that person?
    `the person has previously indicated that the person is interested in offers of that kind` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(3)(b)(iii) the person has previously indicated that the person is interested in offers of that kind` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(3)(b) the offer is made to a person who is likely to be interested in that offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is likely to be interested in that offer`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is made to a person who is likely to be interested in that offer"
        IF `there was previous contact before the date of the offer between the person making the offer and that person` OR `there was a previous professional or other connection established before that date between the person making the offer and that person` OR (`the person has previously indicated that the person is interested in offers of that kind` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "having regard to" names three matters and does not say the likelihood may rest on those alone
    -- FORK s272A-3b | s 272A(3)(b) | `s 272A(3)(b) the offer is made to a person who is likely to be interested in that offer` | took the likelihood as a judgment the person states, answered JUST TRUE only when it rests on at least one of the three matters (i), (ii), (iii), and NOTHING when the person is likely to be interested but none of the three is shown | other reading JUST TRUE on the judgment alone, or JUST FALSE when none of the three holds | licence {IN-SHORT} ("having regard to" is not "only"); under "Marginal readings for a lawyer"

-- src:42810 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1), a personal offer of securities
-- src:42811 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts is one that —
@ref s 272A(3) (src:42810-42811)
GIVEN
    `the offer may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made, as section 272A(3)(a) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(3)(a) the offer may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the offer is made to a person who is likely to be interested in that offer, as section 272A(3)(b) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(3)(b) the offer is made to a person who is likely to be interested in that offer` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(3) the offer is a personal offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the offer may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made, as section 272A(3)(a) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the offer is made to a person who is likely to be interested in that offer, as section 272A(3)(b) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a personal offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts is one that"
        IF (`the offer may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made, as section 272A(3)(a) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the offer is made to a person who is likely to be interested in that offer, as section 272A(3)(b) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (a) or (b) is not answered

-- src:42802 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b), where any notice,
-- src:42803 | circular, material, publication or other document is issued in
-- src:42804 | connection with the offer, the person making the offer is deemed to
-- src:42805 | have given the statement and notification to the person to whom the
-- src:42806 | offer is made in accordance with that provision if such statement or
-- src:42807 | notification is contained in the first page of that notice, circular,
-- src:42808 | material, publication or document.
@ref s 272A(2) (src:42802-42808)
GIVEN
    `a notice, circular, material, publication or other document is issued in connection with the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a notice, circular, material, publication or other document issued in connection with the offer?
    `the statement and notification are contained in the first page of that notice, circular, material, publication or document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the statement and the notification contained in the first page of that notice, circular, material, publication or document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(2) the statement and notification are treated as given` MEANS
    IF `a notice, circular, material, publication or other document is issued in connection with the offer` AND `the statement and notification are contained in the first page of that notice, circular, material, publication or document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is deemed to have given the statement and notification to the person to whom the offer is made in accordance with that provision if such statement or notification is contained in the first page"
    -- FORK s272A-2 | s 272A(2) | `s 272A(2) the statement and notification are treated as given` | took NOTHING where the deeming condition is not met (the deeming is an aid; the person may still have given the statement and notification by other means, which paragraph (1)(b) asks as its own facts) | other reading JUST FALSE ("if" condition) | licence {IN-SHORT} against {G1}: the provision grants a deeming, so a failed gate is not read as a bar

-- src:42688 | (a) the total amount raised by the person from such offers
-- src:42689 | within any period of 12 months does not exceed —
-- src:42691 | (i) $5 million (or its equivalent in a foreign currency); or
-- src:42693 | (ii) such other amount as the Authority may prescribe in
-- src:42694 | substitution for the amount specified in
-- src:42695 | sub‑paragraph (i);
@ref s 272A(1)(a) (src:42688-42695)
GIVEN
    `the total amount raised by the person from such offers within the period of 12 months, in Singapore dollars or the equivalent in a foreign currency` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount raised by the person from such offers within the period of 12 months, in Singapore dollars (or the equivalent in a foreign currency)? Count it as sections 272A(4) and (5) direct.
    `the Authority has prescribed another amount in substitution for $5 million` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed another amount in substitution for $5 million (or its equivalent in a foreign currency)?
    `the other amount the Authority has prescribed in substitution` IS A NUMBER @desc What other amount has the Authority prescribed in substitution for $5 million, in the same currency as the total? (Put 0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(1)(a) the total amount raised within the period of 12 months does not exceed the limit` MEANS
    IF `the total amount raised by the person from such offers within the period of 12 months, in Singapore dollars or the equivalent in a foreign currency` AT MOST (IF `the Authority has prescribed another amount in substitution for $5 million` THEN `the other amount the Authority has prescribed in substitution` ELSE 5000000)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the total amount raised by the person from such offers within any period of 12 months does not exceed"
    -- FORK s272A-1a | s 272A(1)(a) | `s 272A(1)(a) the total amount raised within the period of 12 months does not exceed the limit` | took "within any period of 12 months" as a window the caller names: the function answers for one window, and the exemption holds only if it holds for every window (the caller asks once for each window) | other reading a single trailing window ending on the offer date | licence the text's own "any period of 12 months". The "$5 million (or its equivalent in a foreign currency)" is read as the same limit in whichever currency the total is stated: the caller states the total in one currency.

-- src:42697 | (b) in respect of each offer, the person making the offer gives
-- src:42698 | the person to whom the offer is made —
-- src:42700 | (i) a statement in writing that states —
-- src:42702 | (A) where units or derivatives of units in a business
-- src:42703 | trust are being offered and the business trust is
-- src:42704 | not registered under the Business Trusts
-- src:42705 | Act 2004 —
-- src:42707 | “This offer is made in reliance on the
-- src:42708 | exemption under section 272A(1) of the
-- src:42709 | Securities and Futures Act 2001. It is not
-- src:42710 | made in or accompanied by a prospectus
-- src:42711 | that is registered by the Monetary
-- src:42712 | Authority of Singapore and the business
-- src:42713 | trust is not registered under the Business
-- src:42714 | Trusts Act 2004.”; and
-- src:42716 | (B) in any other case —
-- src:42718 | “This offer is made in reliance on the
-- src:42719 | exemption under section 272A(1) of the
-- src:42720 | Securities and Futures Act 2001. It is not
-- src:42721 | made in or accompanied by a prospectus
-- src:42722 | that is registered by the Monetary
-- src:42723 | Authority of Singapore.”; and
@ref s 272A(1)(b)(i) (src:42697-42723)
GIVEN
    `a statement in writing has been given to the person to whom the offer is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer given the person to whom the offer is made a statement in writing?
    `the statement and notification are treated as given under section 272A(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(2) the statement and notification are treated as given` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `units or derivatives of units in a business trust are being offered and the business trust is not registered under the Business Trusts Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are units or derivatives of units in a business trust being offered, and is the business trust not registered under the Business Trusts Act 2004?
    `the statement states the words set out in sub-paragraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state the words set out in section 272A(1)(b)(i)(A) ("This offer is made in reliance on the exemption under section 272A(1) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001. It is not made in or accompanied by a prospectus that is registered by the Monetary Authority of Singapore and the business trust is not registered under the Business Trusts Act 2004.")?
    `the statement states the words set out in sub-paragraph (B)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state the words set out in section 272A(1)(b)(i)(B) ("This offer is made in reliance on the exemption under section 272A(1) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001. It is not made in or accompanied by a prospectus that is registered by the Monetary Authority of Singapore.")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(1)(b)(i) the statement in writing is given as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (`a statement in writing has been given to the person to whom the offer is made` OR (`the statement and notification are treated as given under section 272A(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND (IF `units or derivatives of units in a business trust are being offered and the business trust is not registered under the Business Trusts Act 2004` THEN `the statement states the words set out in sub-paragraph (A)` ELSE `the statement states the words set out in sub-paragraph (B)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of each offer, the person making the offer gives the person to whom the offer is made — (i) a statement in writing that states"

-- src:42728 | (ii) a notification in writing that the securities or
-- src:42729 | securities‑based derivatives contracts to which the
-- src:42730 | offer (called in this sub‑paragraph the initial offer)
-- src:42731 | relates must not be subsequently sold to any person,
-- src:42732 | unless the offer resulting in such subsequent sale is
-- src:42733 | made —
-- src:42735 | (A) in compliance with Subdivisions (1A), (2) and
-- src:42736 | (3) of this Division;
-- src:42740 | (B) in reliance on subsection (8)(c) or any other
-- src:42741 | exemption under any provision of this
-- src:42742 | Subdivision (other than this subsection); or
-- src:42744 | (C) where at least 6 months have elapsed from the
-- src:42745 | date the securities or securities‑based
-- src:42746 | derivatives contracts were acquired under the
-- src:42747 | initial offer, in reliance on the exemption under
-- src:42748 | this subsection;
@ref s 272A(1)(b)(ii) (src:42728-42748)
GIVEN
    `a notification in writing has been given to the person to whom the offer is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer given the person to whom the offer is made a notification in writing that the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts must not be subsequently sold to any person unless the offer resulting in the sale is made as sub-paragraph (ii) lists?
    `the statement and notification are treated as given under section 272A(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(2) the statement and notification are treated as given` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the notification names compliance with Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification name an offer made in compliance with Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of Division 1 of Part 13?
    `the notification names reliance on subsection (8)(c) or any other exemption under this Subdivision other than subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification name an offer made in reliance on section 272A(8)(c) or any other exemption under Subdivision (4) other than section 272A(1)?
    `the notification names the case where at least 6 months have elapsed from the date the securities were acquired under the initial offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification name an offer made, where at least 6 months have elapsed from the date the securities or contracts were acquired under the initial offer, in reliance on the exemption under section 272A(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(1)(b)(ii) the notification in writing is given as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (`a notification in writing has been given to the person to whom the offer is made` OR (`the statement and notification are treated as given under section 272A(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND `the notification names compliance with Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division` AND `the notification names reliance on subsection (8)(c) or any other exemption under this Subdivision other than subsection (1)` AND `the notification names the case where at least 6 months have elapsed from the date the securities were acquired under the initial offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) a notification in writing that the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts to which the offer"
    -- FORK s272A-1bii | s 272A(1)(b)(ii) | `s 272A(1)(b)(ii) the notification in writing is given as the paragraph requires` | took the notification as one that names all three ways (A), (B) and (C) of a lawful later sale, as the text words it | other reading a notification that names fewer of them still states the restriction | licence the text's own wording of the notification (the sub-paragraphs are joined by "or" inside the notification, so each names a case the notification must tell the buyer of)

-- src:42697 | (b) in respect of each offer, the person making the offer gives
-- src:42698 | the person to whom the offer is made —
@ref s 272A(1)(b) (src:42697-42698)
GIVEN
    `the statement in writing is given as the paragraph requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(1)(b)(i) the statement in writing is given as the paragraph requires` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the notification in writing is given as the paragraph requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(1)(b)(ii) the notification in writing is given as the paragraph requires` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(1)(b) the person making each offer gives the statement and the notification` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the statement in writing is given as the paragraph requires` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the notification in writing is given as the paragraph requires` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of each offer, the person making the offer gives the person to whom the offer is made"
        IF (`the statement in writing is given as the paragraph requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the notification in writing is given as the paragraph requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the statement or the notification is not answered

-- src:42786 | (e) no prospectus in respect of any of the offers has been
-- src:42787 | registered by the Authority or, where a prospectus has been
-- src:42788 | registered —
-- src:42790 | (i) the prospectus has expired pursuant to section 250;
-- src:42791 | or
-- src:42793 | (ii) the person making the offer has before making the
-- src:42794 | offer informed the Authority by written notice of its
-- src:42795 | intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption
-- src:42796 | under this subsection.
@ref s 272A(1)(e) (src:42786-42796)
GIVEN
    `a prospectus in respect of any of the offers has been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered a prospectus in respect of any of the offers?
    `the prospectus has expired under section 250` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prospectus expired pursuant to section 250? (Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (2), another part's answer.)
    `the person making the offer has before making the offer informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer, before making the offer, informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under section 272A(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(1)(e) no prospectus is registered, or the registered prospectus has expired or the Authority has been told` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a prospectus in respect of any of the offers has been registered by the Authority`) OR `the prospectus has expired under section 250` OR `the person making the offer has before making the offer informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under this subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no prospectus in respect of any of the offers has been registered by the Authority or, where a prospectus has been registered"

-- src:42683 | 272A.—(1) Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other
-- src:42684 | than section 257) do not apply to personal offers of securities or
-- src:42685 | securities‑based derivatives contracts of an entity or a business trust
-- src:42686 | by a person if —
@ref s 272A(1) (src:42683-42686)
GIVEN
    `the offer is a personal offer, as section 272A(3) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(3) the offer is a personal offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (a), the amount raised` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(1)(a) the total amount raised within the period of 12 months does not exceed the limit` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (b), the statement and notification` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(1)(b) the person making each offer gives the statement and the notification` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (c), no advertisement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(1)(c) none of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (d), the selling or promotional expenses` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(1)(d) the selling or promotional expenses are ones the exemption allows` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (e), the prospectus` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(1)(e) no prospectus is registered, or the registered prospectus has expired or the Authority has been told` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offer is a personal offer, as section 272A(3) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "do not apply to personal offers of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of an entity or a business trust by a person if"
        IF (`paragraph (a), the amount raised` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (b), the statement and notification` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (c), no advertisement` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (d), the selling or promotional expenses` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (e), the prospectus` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to personal offers of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of an entity or a business trust by a person if"
        IF (`the offer is a personal offer, as section 272A(3) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (a), the amount raised` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (b), the statement and notification` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (c), no advertisement` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (d), the selling or promotional expenses` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (e), the prospectus` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a paragraph or the personal offer is not answered
    -- FORK s272A-1 | s 272A(1) | `s 272A(1) the offer is exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` | took NOTHING where the offer is not a personal offer (a scope limit with no "only"), JUST FALSE where a paragraph (a) to (e) fails (conditions of an "if"), JUST TRUE only when all hold | other reading NOTHING for a failed paragraph ("if A then B" does not say "if not A then not B") and JUST FALSE for a non-personal offer | licence {P-c} for the first, {IN-SHORT} for the second; the second is under "Marginal readings for a lawyer". Section 257 and the Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) are another part's; this function answers only "is the offer exempt from them".

-- src:42890 | (4) In determining the amount raised by an offer, the following
-- src:42891 | must be included:
-- src:42893 | (a) the amount payable for the securities or securities‑based
-- src:42894 | derivatives contracts at the time they are allotted, issued or
-- src:42895 | sold;
-- src:42897 | (b) if the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:42898 | are issued partly‑paid, any amount payable at a future time
-- src:42899 | if a call is made;
-- src:42901 | (c) if the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:42902 | carry a right (by whatever name called) to be converted
-- src:42903 | into other securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:42904 | contracts or to acquire other securities or securities‑based
-- src:42905 | derivatives contracts, any amount payable on the exercise
-- src:42906 | of the right to convert them into, or to acquire, other
-- src:42907 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts.
@ref s 272A(4) (src:42890-42907)
GIVEN
    `the amount payable for the securities or contracts at the time they are allotted, issued or sold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount payable for the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts at the time they are allotted, issued or sold?
    `the amount payable at a future time if a call is made, where the securities or contracts are issued partly paid` IS A NUMBER @desc If the securities or contracts are issued partly paid, what amount is payable at a future time if a call is made? (Put 0 if they are not partly paid.)
    `the amount payable on the exercise of a right to convert them into, or to acquire, other securities or contracts` IS A NUMBER @desc If the securities or contracts carry a right to be converted into other securities or contracts, or to acquire them, what amount is payable on the exercise of the right? (Put 0 if there is no such right.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 272A(4) the amount raised by an offer` MEANS
    (`the amount payable for the securities or contracts at the time they are allotted, issued or sold` PLUS `the amount payable at a future time if a call is made, where the securities or contracts are issued partly paid`) PLUS `the amount payable on the exercise of a right to convert them into, or to acquire, other securities or contracts`

DECLARE `s 272A(5) an earlier offer` HAS
    `the day of the earlier offer` IS A DATE
    `the amount raised by the earlier offer` IS A NUMBER
    `the earlier offer was made by that person of securities issued by the same entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earlier offer was a closely related offer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earlier offer was made in reliance on the exemption under section 272A(1) or section 302B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:42911 | (5) In determining whether the amount raised by a person from
-- src:42912 | offers within a period of 12 months exceeds the applicable amount
-- src:42913 | mentioned in subsection (1)(a), each amount raised —
-- src:42918 | (a) by that person from any offer of securities or
-- src:42919 | securities‑based derivatives contracts issued by the same
-- src:42920 | entity; or
-- src:42922 | (b) by that person or another person from any offer of
-- src:42923 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of an
-- src:42924 | entity or a business trust, or units in a collective investment
-- src:42925 | scheme, which is a closely related offer,
-- src:42927 | if any, within that period in reliance on the exemption under
-- src:42928 | subsection (1) or section 302B(1) must be included.
@ref s 272A(5) (src:42911-42928)
GIVEN
    `the first day of the period of 12 months asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period of 12 months asked about?
    `the earlier offers` IS A LIST OF `s 272A(5) an earlier offer` @desc For each earlier offer the person or another person made: the day, the amount raised, whether it was made by that person of securities issued by the same entity, whether it was a closely related offer, and whether it relied on the exemption under section 272A(1) or section 302B(1). (An empty list: none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 272A(5) the amounts raised by earlier offers that must be included` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier offers`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN o FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF (o's `the earlier offer was made in reliance on the exemption under section 272A(1) or section 302B(1)`) AND ((o's `the earlier offer was made by that person of securities issued by the same entity`) OR (o's `the earlier offer was a closely related offer`)) AND (o's `the day of the earlier offer` AT LEAST `the first day of the period of 12 months asked about`) AND (o's `the day of the earlier offer` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the first day of the period of 12 months asked about` 12 Months))
        THEN (o's `the amount raised by the earlier offer`) PLUS (`s 272A(5) the amounts raised by earlier offers that must be included` `the first day of the period of 12 months asked about` rest)
        ELSE `s 272A(5) the amounts raised by earlier offers that must be included` `the first day of the period of 12 months asked about` rest
    -- FORK s272A-5 | s 272A(5) | `s 272A(5) the amounts raised by earlier offers that must be included` | took the two limbs (a) and (b) as alternatives joined by "or", each counted only "within that period in reliance on the exemption under subsection (1) or section 302B(1)", and the period as 12 months beginning on the first day asked about | other reading an earlier offer counts whether or not it relied on the exemption | licence the text's own "if any, within that period in reliance on the exemption". The function adds amounts; it never answers JUST FALSE.

GIVEN
    `the amount raised by the offer, as section 272A(4) counts it` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount does the offer raise, counted as section 272A(4) directs?
    `the amounts raised by earlier offers that must be included, as section 272A(5) counts them` IS A NUMBER @desc What total of earlier amounts must be included, as section 272A(5) directs?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 272A(5) the total amount raised within the period of 12 months` MEANS
    `the amount raised by the offer, as section 272A(4) counts it` PLUS `the amounts raised by earlier offers that must be included, as section 272A(5) counts them`

-- src:42932 | (6) Whether an offer is a closely related offer under subsection (5)
-- src:42933 | is determined by considering such factors as the Authority may
-- src:42934 | prescribe.
@ref s 272A(6) (src:42932-42934)
GIVEN
    `the offer is a closely related offer on the factors the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer, on considering the factors the Authority has prescribed, a closely related offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(6) the offer is a closely related offer` MEANS
    IF `the offer is a closely related offer on the factors the Authority has prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "is determined by considering such factors as the Authority may prescribe"

-- src:42936 | (7) For the purpose of this section, an offer of securities or
-- src:42937 | securities‑based derivatives contracts made by a person acting as an
-- src:42938 | agent of another person is treated as an offer made by that other
-- src:42939 | person.
@ref s 272A(7) (src:42936-42939)
GIVEN
    `the offer is made by a person acting as an agent of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made by a person acting as an agent of another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(7) the offer is treated as made by that other person` MEANS
    IF `the offer is made by a person acting as an agent of another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of an offer made by an agent

§ `s 272A: small offers (the resale of what was acquired under the exemption: subsections (8) and (9))`

-- src:42952 | (a) such offer is made in reliance on an exemption under any
-- src:42953 | provision of this Subdivision (other than this section);
@ref s 272A(8)(a) (src:42952-42953)
GIVEN
    `the subsequent offer is made in reliance on an exemption under a provision of this Subdivision other than section 272A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer from the person who acquired the securities to the other person made in reliance on an exemption under any provision of Subdivision (4) other than section 272A?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(8)(a) the subsequent offer is made in reliance on another exemption of this Subdivision` MEANS
    IF `the subsequent offer is made in reliance on an exemption under a provision of this Subdivision other than section 272A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless — (a) such offer is made in reliance on an exemption under any provision of this Subdivision (other than this section)"

-- src:42955 | (b) such offer is made in reliance on an exemption under
-- src:42956 | subsection (1) and at least 6 months have elapsed from the
-- src:42957 | date the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:42958 | were acquired under the initial offer; or
@ref s 272A(8)(b) (src:42955-42958)
GIVEN
    `the subsequent offer is made in reliance on an exemption under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer from the person who acquired the securities to the other person made in reliance on the exemption under section 272A(1)?
    `the day the securities or contracts were acquired under the initial offer` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts acquired under the initial offer?
    `the day of the subsequent offer` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the subsequent offer made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(8)(b) the subsequent offer is made in reliance on subsection (1) and at least 6 months have elapsed` MEANS
    IF `the subsequent offer is made in reliance on an exemption under subsection (1)` AND (`the day of the subsequent offer` GREATER THAN (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the securities or contracts were acquired under the initial offer` 6 Months))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) such offer is made in reliance on an exemption under subsection (1) and at least 6 months have elapsed from the date the securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts were acquired under the initial offer"
    -- FORK s272A-8b | s 272A(8)(b) | `s 272A(8)(b) the subsequent offer is made in reliance on subsection (1) and at least 6 months have elapsed` | took "at least 6 months have elapsed from the date acquired" as: the offer is made after the last day of the period of 6 months that follows the day of acquisition (convention P1 of the keel: the day of the event is not counted, so 6 months from 1 January end on 1 July and the first day after is 2 July) | other reading the offer is in time on the corresponding date itself (1 July) | licence the keel's P1 and P10; "elapsed" is read as the whole period having run

-- src:42960 | (c) such offer is one —
-- src:42962 | (i) that may be accepted only by the person to whom it is
-- src:42963 | made;
@ref s 272A(8)(c)(i) (src:42960-42963)
GIVEN
    `the subsequent offer may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the subsequent offer be accepted only by the person to whom it is made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(8)(c)(i) the subsequent offer may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made` MEANS
    IF `the subsequent offer may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) such offer is one — (i) that may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made"

-- src:42979 | (C) any previous indication (whether through
-- src:42980 | statements made or actions carried out)
-- src:42981 | before that date by that person that indicate
-- src:42982 | to any of the following persons that that person
-- src:42983 | is interested in offers of that kind:
-- src:42985 | (CA) the person making the initial offer;
-- src:42987 | (CB) the holder of a capital markets services
-- src:42988 | licence to deal in capital markets
-- src:42989 | products that are securities or
-- src:42990 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:42992 | (CC) an exempt person in respect of dealing
-- src:42993 | in capital markets products that are
-- src:42994 | securities or securities‑based
-- src:42995 | derivatives contracts;
-- src:42997 | (CD) a person licensed under the Financial
-- src:42998 | Advisers Act 2001 in respect of the
-- src:42999 | provision of financial advisory services
-- src:43000 | concerning investment products;
-- src:43002 | (CE) an exempt financial adviser as defined
-- src:43003 | in section 2(1) of the Financial
-- src:43004 | Advisers Act 2001;
-- src:43006 | (CF) a person who is licensed, approved,
-- src:43007 | authorised or otherwise regulated under
-- src:43008 | the laws, codes or other requirements of
-- src:43009 | any foreign jurisdiction in respect of
-- src:43010 | dealing in capital markets products that
-- src:43015 | are securities or securities‑based
-- src:43016 | derivatives contracts;
-- src:43018 | (CG) a person who is exempt from the laws,
-- src:43019 | codes or requirements mentioned in
-- src:43020 | sub‑paragraph (CF) in respect of
-- src:43021 | dealing in capital markets products
-- src:43022 | that are securities or securities‑based
-- src:43023 | derivatives contracts;
-- src:43025 | (CH) a person who is licensed, approved,
-- src:43026 | authorised or otherwise regulated under
-- src:43027 | the laws, codes or other requirements of
-- src:43028 | any foreign jurisdiction in respect of
-- src:43029 | the provision of financial advisory
-- src:43030 | services concerning investment
-- src:43031 | products;
-- src:43033 | (CI) a person who is exempt from the laws,
-- src:43034 | codes or requirements mentioned in
-- src:43035 | sub‑paragraph (CH) in respect of the
-- src:43036 | provision of financial advisory services
-- src:43037 | concerning investment products;
@ref s 272A(8)(c)(ii)(C) (src:42979-43037)
GIVEN
    `the person has previously indicated to the person making the initial offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person, by statements or actions before the date of the offer, indicate to the person making the initial offer that the person is interested in offers of that kind?
    `the person has previously indicated to the holder of a capital markets services licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person, by statements or actions before the date of the offer, indicate to the holder of a capital markets services licence to deal in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts that the person is interested in offers of that kind?
    `the person has previously indicated to an exempt person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person, by statements or actions before the date of the offer, indicate to an exempt person in respect of dealing in capital markets products that are securities or securities-based derivatives contracts that the person is interested in offers of that kind?
    `the person has previously indicated to a person licensed under the Financial Advisers Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person, by statements or actions before the date of the offer, indicate to a person licensed under the Financial Advisers Act 2001 in respect of the provision of financial advisory services concerning investment products that the person is interested in offers of that kind?
    `the person has previously indicated to an exempt financial adviser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person, by statements or actions before the date of the offer, indicate to an exempt financial adviser as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001 that the person is interested in offers of that kind?
    `the person has previously indicated to a person described in sub-paragraph (CF), (CG), (CH) or (CI)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(3)(b)(iii)(F) the person to whom the indication was made is a foreign regulated or exempt person` answer for the person to whom the indication was made (the persons in (CF) to (CI) are the same four kinds)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(8)(c)(ii)(C) the person has previously indicated that the person is interested in offers of that kind` MEANS
    `s 272A(3)(b)(iii) the person has previously indicated that the person is interested in offers of that kind` `the person has previously indicated to the person making the initial offer` `the person has previously indicated to the holder of a capital markets services licence` `the person has previously indicated to an exempt person` `the person has previously indicated to a person licensed under the Financial Advisers Act 2001` `the person has previously indicated to an exempt financial adviser` `the person has previously indicated to a person described in sub-paragraph (CF), (CG), (CH) or (CI)`
    -- The list of persons in (CA) to (CI) is the list of (A) to (F) of section 272A(3)(b)(iii) with the person making the initial offer in place of the person making the offer; the one function answers both.

-- src:42968 | (ii) that is made to a person who is likely to be interested
-- src:42969 | in the offer having regard to —
-- src:42971 | (A) any previous contact before the date of the
-- src:42972 | offer between the person making the initial
-- src:42973 | offer and that person;
-- src:42975 | (B) any previous professional or other connection
-- src:42976 | established before that date between the person
-- src:42977 | making the initial offer and that person; or
@ref s 272A(8)(c)(ii) (src:42968-42977)
GIVEN
    `the person is likely to be interested in the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the subsequent offer is made likely to be interested in the offer?
    `there was previous contact before the date of the offer between the person making the initial offer and that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there any previous contact before the date of the offer between the person making the initial offer and that person?
    `there was a previous professional or other connection established before that date between the person making the initial offer and that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there any previous professional or other connection established before the date of the offer between the person making the initial offer and that person?
    `the person has previously indicated that the person is interested in offers of that kind` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(8)(c)(ii)(C) the person has previously indicated that the person is interested in offers of that kind` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(8)(c)(ii) the subsequent offer is made to a person likely to be interested in the offer` MEANS
    `s 272A(3)(b) the offer is made to a person who is likely to be interested in that offer` `the person is likely to be interested in the offer` `there was previous contact before the date of the offer between the person making the initial offer and that person` `there was a previous professional or other connection established before that date between the person making the initial offer and that person` `the person has previously indicated that the person is interested in offers of that kind`

-- src:43039 | (iii) in respect of which the firstmentioned person has
-- src:43040 | given the second‑mentioned person —
-- src:43042 | (A) a statement in writing that states —
-- src:43044 | (AA) where units or derivatives of units in a
-- src:43045 | business trust are being offered and the
-- src:43046 | business trust is not registered under
-- src:43047 | the Business Trusts Act 2004 —
-- src:43049 | “This offer is made in reliance on
-- src:43051 | the exemption under
-- src:43053 | section 272A(8)(c) of the
-- src:43055 | Securities and Futures Act 2001.
-- src:43057 | It is not made in or accompanied
-- src:43059 | by a prospectus that is registered
-- src:43061 | by the Monetary Authority of
-- src:43063 | Singapore and the business trust
-- src:43068 | is not registered under the
-- src:43069 | Business Trusts Act 2004.”; and
-- src:43071 | (AB) in any other case —
-- src:43073 | “This offer is made in reliance on
-- src:43075 | the exemption under
-- src:43077 | section 272A(8)(c) of the
-- src:43079 | Securities and Futures Act 2001.
-- src:43081 | It is not made in or accompanied
-- src:43083 | by a prospectus that is registered
-- src:43085 | by the Monetary Authority of
-- src:43087 | Singapore.”;
-- src:43089 | (B) a notification in writing that the securities or
-- src:43090 | securities‑based derivatives contracts being
-- src:43091 | offered must not be subsequently sold to any
-- src:43092 | person unless the offer resulting in such
-- src:43093 | subsequent sale is made —
-- src:43095 | (BA) in compliance with Subdivisions (2)
-- src:43096 | and (3) of this Division;
-- src:43098 | (BB) in reliance on this subsection or any
-- src:43099 | other exemption under any provision of
-- src:43100 | this Subdivision (other than
-- src:43101 | subsection (1)); or
-- src:43103 | (BC) where at least 6 months have elapsed
-- src:43104 | from the date the securities or
-- src:43105 | securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:43106 | were acquired under the initial offer,
-- src:43107 | in reliance on the exemption under
-- src:43108 | subsection (1);
@ref s 272A(8)(c)(iii) (src:43039-43108)
GIVEN
    `a statement in writing has been given to the person to whom the subsequent offer is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who made the subsequent offer given the person to whom the offer is made a statement in writing?
    `the statement and notification are treated as given under section 272A(9)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(9) the statement and notification in subsection (8)(c)(iii) are treated as given` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `units or derivatives of units in a business trust are being offered and the business trust is not registered under the Business Trusts Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are units or derivatives of units in a business trust being offered, and is the business trust not registered under the Business Trusts Act 2004?
    `the statement states the words set out in sub-paragraph (AA)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state the words set out in section 272A(8)(c)(iii)(A)(AA) ("This offer is made in reliance on the exemption under section 272A(8)(c) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001. It is not made in or accompanied by a prospectus that is registered by the Monetary Authority of Singapore and the business trust is not registered under the Business Trusts Act 2004.")?
    `the statement states the words set out in sub-paragraph (AB)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement state the words set out in section 272A(8)(c)(iii)(A)(AB) ("This offer is made in reliance on the exemption under section 272A(8)(c) of the Securities and Futures Act 2001. It is not made in or accompanied by a prospectus that is registered by the Monetary Authority of Singapore.")?
    `a notification in writing has been given to the person to whom the subsequent offer is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person who made the subsequent offer given the person to whom the offer is made a notification in writing that the securities or contracts must not be subsequently sold to any person unless the offer resulting in the sale is made as sub-paragraph (B) lists?
    `the notification names compliance with Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification name an offer made in compliance with Subdivisions (2) and (3) of Division 1 of Part 13?
    `the notification names reliance on this subsection or any other exemption under this Subdivision other than subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification name an offer made in reliance on section 272A(8) or any other exemption under Subdivision (4) other than section 272A(1)?
    `the notification names the case where at least 6 months have elapsed from the date the securities were acquired under the initial offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notification name an offer made, where at least 6 months have elapsed from the date the securities or contracts were acquired under the initial offer, in reliance on the exemption under section 272A(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(8)(c)(iii) the statement and notification are given` MEANS
    IF ((`a statement in writing has been given to the person to whom the subsequent offer is made` AND `a notification in writing has been given to the person to whom the subsequent offer is made`) OR (`the statement and notification are treated as given under section 272A(9)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND (IF `units or derivatives of units in a business trust are being offered and the business trust is not registered under the Business Trusts Act 2004` THEN `the statement states the words set out in sub-paragraph (AA)` ELSE `the statement states the words set out in sub-paragraph (AB)`) AND `the notification names compliance with Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division` AND `the notification names reliance on this subsection or any other exemption under this Subdivision other than subsection (1)` AND `the notification names the case where at least 6 months have elapsed from the date the securities were acquired under the initial offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of which the firstmentioned person has given the second‑mentioned person — (A) a statement in writing that states"

-- src:43148 | (9) Subsection (2) applies, with the necessary modifications, in
-- src:43149 | relation to the statement and notification referred to in
-- src:43150 | subsection (8)(c)(iii).
@ref s 272A(9) (src:43148-43150)
GIVEN
    `a notice, circular, material, publication or other document is issued in connection with the subsequent offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a notice, circular, material, publication or other document issued in connection with the subsequent offer?
    `the statement and notification are contained in the first page of that notice, circular, material, publication or document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the statement and the notification contained in the first page of that notice, circular, material, publication or document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(9) the statement and notification in subsection (8)(c)(iii) are treated as given` MEANS
    `s 272A(2) the statement and notification are treated as given` `a notice, circular, material, publication or other document is issued in connection with the subsequent offer` `the statement and notification are contained in the first page of that notice, circular, material, publication or document`

-- src:43110 | (iv) that is not accompanied by an advertisement making
-- src:43111 | an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended
-- src:43112 | offer; and
@ref s 272A(8)(c)(iv) (src:43110-43112)
GIVEN
    `the subsequent offer is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subsequent offer accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(8)(c)(iv) the subsequent offer is not accompanied by an advertisement` MEANS
    IF `the subsequent offer is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that is not accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:43114 | (v) in respect of which no selling or promotional
-- src:43115 | expenses are paid or incurred in connection with
-- src:43116 | the offer other than those incurred for administrative
-- src:43121 | or professional services, or by way of commission or
-- src:43122 | fee for services rendered by —
-- src:43124 | (A) the holder of a capital markets services licence
-- src:43125 | to deal in capital markets products that are
-- src:43126 | securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:43127 | contracts;
-- src:43129 | (B) an exempt person in respect of dealing in
-- src:43130 | capital markets products that are securities or
-- src:43131 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:43133 | (C) a person who is licensed, approved, authorised
-- src:43134 | or otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or
-- src:43135 | other requirements of any foreign jurisdiction
-- src:43136 | in respect of dealing in capital markets
-- src:43137 | products that are securities or securities‑based
-- src:43138 | derivatives contracts; or
-- src:43140 | (D) a person who is exempt from the laws, codes or
-- src:43141 | requirements mentioned in sub‑paragraph (C)
-- src:43142 | in respect of dealing in capital markets
-- src:43143 | products that are securities or securities‑based
-- src:43144 | derivatives contracts.
@ref s 272A(8)(c)(v) (src:43114-43144)
GIVEN
    `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the subsequent offer` IS A LIST OF `s 272A(1)(d) kind of selling or promotional expense` @desc What are the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the subsequent offer? (An empty list: none are paid or incurred.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(8)(c)(v) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred other than those the paragraph allows` MEANS
    `s 272A(1)(d) the selling or promotional expenses are ones the exemption allows` `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with the subsequent offer`

-- src:42960 | (c) such offer is one —
@ref s 272A(8)(c) (src:42960-42960)
GIVEN
    `sub-paragraph (i), accepted only by the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(8)(c)(i) the subsequent offer may be accepted only by the person to whom it is made` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `sub-paragraph (ii), likely to be interested` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(8)(c)(ii) the subsequent offer is made to a person likely to be interested in the offer` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `sub-paragraph (iii), the statement and notification` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(8)(c)(iii) the statement and notification are given` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `sub-paragraph (iv), no advertisement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(8)(c)(iv) the subsequent offer is not accompanied by an advertisement` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `sub-paragraph (v), the selling or promotional expenses` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(8)(c)(v) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred other than those the paragraph allows` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(8)(c) the subsequent offer is one that meets sub-paragraphs (i) to (v)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`sub-paragraph (i), accepted only by the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`sub-paragraph (ii), likely to be interested` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`sub-paragraph (iii), the statement and notification` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`sub-paragraph (iv), no advertisement` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`sub-paragraph (v), the selling or promotional expenses` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) such offer is one"
        IF (`sub-paragraph (i), accepted only by the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`sub-paragraph (ii), likely to be interested` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`sub-paragraph (iii), the statement and notification` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`sub-paragraph (iv), no advertisement` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`sub-paragraph (v), the selling or promotional expenses` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a sub-paragraph is not answered

-- src:42943 | (8) Where securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:42944 | acquired through an offer made in reliance on the exemption under
-- src:42945 | subsection (1) (called in this subsection an initial offer) are
-- src:42946 | subsequently sold by the person who acquired the securities or
-- src:42947 | securities‑based derivatives contracts to another person,
-- src:42948 | Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division apply to the offer from
-- src:42949 | the firstmentioned person to the second‑mentioned person which
-- src:42950 | resulted in that sale, unless —
@ref s 272A(8) (src:42943-42950)
GIVEN
    `the securities or contracts were acquired through an offer made in reliance on the exemption under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts acquired through an offer made in reliance on the exemption under section 272A(1) (the initial offer)?
    `the securities or contracts are subsequently sold by the person who acquired them to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the securities or contracts subsequently sold by the person who acquired them to another person?
    `paragraph (a), another exemption of this Subdivision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(8)(a) the subsequent offer is made in reliance on another exemption of this Subdivision` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (b), subsection (1) and 6 months` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(8)(b) the subsequent offer is made in reliance on subsection (1) and at least 6 months have elapsed` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (c), the offer is one that meets sub-paragraphs (i) to (v)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272A(8)(c) the subsequent offer is one that meets sub-paragraphs (i) to (v)` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272A(8) Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division apply to the offer that resulted in the sale` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the securities or contracts were acquired through an offer made in reliance on the exemption under subsection (1)` AND `the securities or contracts are subsequently sold by the person who acquired them to another person`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts acquired through an offer made in reliance on the exemption under subsection (1) (called in this subsection an initial offer) are subsequently sold by the person who acquired"
        IF (`paragraph (a), another exemption of this Subdivision` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`paragraph (b), subsection (1) and 6 months` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`paragraph (c), the offer is one that meets sub-paragraphs (i) to (v)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless"
        IF (`paragraph (a), another exemption of this Subdivision` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`paragraph (b), subsection (1) and 6 months` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`paragraph (c), the offer is one that meets sub-paragraphs (i) to (v)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a paragraph is not answered
    -- FORK s272A-8 | s 272A(8) | `s 272A(8) Subdivisions (2) and (3) of this Division apply to the offer that resulted in the sale` | took JUST FALSE once an "unless" exception (a), (b) or (c) is met, JUST TRUE when the three exceptions are all unmet, and NOTHING where the securities were not acquired under subsection (1) or were not sold on | other reading NOTHING once an exception is met (the question the text leaves is whether the sale needs a prospectus, which the other Subdivisions answer) | licence {CC} (an "unless" once it is met) and {P-c} for the scope; under "Marginal readings for a lawyer"

§ `s 272B: private placement`

-- src:43280 | (2) The Authority may prescribe such other number of persons in
-- src:43281 | substitution for the number specified in subsection (1)(a).
@ref s 272B(2) (src:43280-43281)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has prescribed another number of persons in substitution for the number specified in subsection (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed another number of persons in substitution for 50?
    `the other number of persons the Authority has prescribed` IS A NUMBER @desc What other number of persons has the Authority prescribed in substitution for 50? (Put 0 if none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 272B(2) the applicable number of persons` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has prescribed another number of persons in substitution for the number specified in subsection (1)(a)`
    THEN `the other number of persons the Authority has prescribed`
    ELSE 50

DECLARE `s 272B(5) kind of offeree` IS ONE OF
    `s 272B(1)(a) an individual or an entity counted as itself`
    `s 272B(5)(a) an entity or a trustee, the entity or trust not formed primarily for the purpose of acquiring the securities`
    `s 272B(5)(b) an entity or a trustee, the entity or trust formed primarily for the purpose of acquiring the securities`
    `s 272B(5)(c) two or more persons who will own the securities as joint owners`
    `s 272B(5)(d) a person acting on behalf of another person`
    `s 272B(5)(f) a person offered with a view to another person acquiring an interest by virtue of section 4`
    `s 272B(5)(g) a person offered with a view to the securities being subsequently offered for sale to another person`

-- src:43310 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (1) —
-- src:43312 | (a) an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:43313 | contracts to an entity or to a trustee is treated as an offer
-- src:43314 | to a single person, provided that the entity or trust is not
-- src:43315 | formed primarily for the purpose of acquiring the securities
-- src:43316 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts which are the
-- src:43317 | subject of the offer;
-- src:43319 | (b) an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:43320 | contracts to an entity or to a trustee is treated as an offer
-- src:43321 | to the equity owners, partners or members of that entity, or
-- src:43322 | to the beneficiaries of the trust (as the case may be) if the
-- src:43323 | entity or trust is formed primarily for the purpose of
-- src:43324 | acquiring the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:43325 | contracts which are the subject of the offer;
-- src:43327 | (c) an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:43328 | contracts to 2 or more persons who will own the
-- src:43329 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:43330 | acquired as joint owners is treated as an offer to a single
-- src:43331 | person;
-- src:43333 | (d) an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:43334 | contracts to a person acting on behalf of another person
-- src:43335 | (whether as an agent or otherwise) is treated as an offer
-- src:43336 | made to that other person;
-- src:43338 | (e) offers of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:43339 | made by a person as an agent of another person is treated as
-- src:43340 | offers made by that other person;
-- src:43342 | (f) where an offer is made to a person with a view to another
-- src:43343 | person acquiring an interest in those securities or
-- src:43344 | securities‑based derivatives contracts by virtue of
-- src:43345 | section 4, only the second‑mentioned person is counted
-- src:43346 | for the purposes of determining whether offers of the
-- src:43347 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts are
-- src:43348 | made to no more than the applicable number of persons
-- src:43349 | specified in subsection (1)(a); and
-- src:43354 | (g) where —
-- src:43356 | (i) an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:43357 | contracts is made to a person in reliance on the
-- src:43358 | exemption under subsection (1) with a view to those
-- src:43359 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:43360 | being subsequently offered for sale to another
-- src:43361 | person; and
-- src:43363 | (ii) that subsequent offer —
-- src:43365 | (A) is not made in reliance on an exemption under
-- src:43366 | any provision of this Subdivision; or
-- src:43368 | (B) is made in reliance on an exemption under
-- src:43369 | subsection (1) or section 280,
-- src:43371 | (g) both persons are counted for the purposes of determining
-- src:43372 | whether offers of the securities or securities‑based
-- src:43373 | derivatives contracts are made to no more than the
-- src:43374 | applicable number of persons specified in
-- src:43375 | subsection (1)(a).
@ref s 272B(5) (src:43310-43375)
GIVEN
    `the kind of the person to whom the offer is made` IS A `s 272B(5) kind of offeree` @desc Which kind of person is the offer made to? (An individual or entity counted as itself, an entity or trustee not formed primarily to acquire the securities, one formed primarily to acquire them, joint owners, a person acting on behalf of another, a person offered with a view to another acquiring an interest by virtue of section 4, or a person offered with a view to a later offer for sale.)
    `the number of equity owners, partners, members or beneficiaries of the entity or trust formed primarily for the purpose of acquiring the securities` IS A NUMBER @desc If the offer is to an entity or trustee formed primarily for the purpose of acquiring the securities: how many equity owners, partners, members or beneficiaries does it have? (Put 0 otherwise.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 272B(5) the number of persons the offer to the offeree counts as` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of the person to whom the offer is made`
    WHEN `s 272B(1)(a) an individual or an entity counted as itself` THEN 1
    WHEN `s 272B(5)(a) an entity or a trustee, the entity or trust not formed primarily for the purpose of acquiring the securities` THEN 1
    WHEN `s 272B(5)(b) an entity or a trustee, the entity or trust formed primarily for the purpose of acquiring the securities` THEN `the number of equity owners, partners, members or beneficiaries of the entity or trust formed primarily for the purpose of acquiring the securities`
    WHEN `s 272B(5)(c) two or more persons who will own the securities as joint owners` THEN 1
    WHEN `s 272B(5)(d) a person acting on behalf of another person` THEN 1
    WHEN `s 272B(5)(f) a person offered with a view to another person acquiring an interest by virtue of section 4` THEN 1
    WHEN `s 272B(5)(g) a person offered with a view to the securities being subsequently offered for sale to another person` THEN 2
    -- FORK s272B-5 | s 272B(5) | `s 272B(5) the number of persons the offer to the offeree counts as` | took each paragraph as a case the caller names; (a), (c), (d) and (f) count as one person (the single person, the joint owners as a single person, the other person on whose behalf, only the second-mentioned person), (b) counts the equity owners, partners, members or beneficiaries, and (g) counts both persons | other reading for (d): the person acting on behalf is itself counted too | licence the text's own words: "treated as an offer to a single person", "treated as an offer made to that other person", "only the second‑mentioned person is counted", "both persons are counted"

@ref s 272B(5)(f) (src:43342-43349)
GIVEN
    `the offer is made to a person with a view to another person acquiring an interest in the securities or contracts by virtue of section 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 4 the person has an interest in the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units` answer for the other person? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272B(5)(f) only the second-mentioned person is counted` MEANS
    IF `the offer is made to a person with a view to another person acquiring an interest in the securities or contracts by virtue of section 4` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where an offer is made to a person with a view to another person acquiring an interest in those securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts by virtue of section 4"

@ref s 272B(5)(g) (src:43354-43375)
GIVEN
    `an offer is made to a person in reliance on the exemption under subsection (1) with a view to the securities being subsequently offered for sale to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an offer made to a person in reliance on the exemption under section 272B(1) with a view to the securities or contracts being subsequently offered for sale to another person?
    `the subsequent offer is not made in reliance on an exemption under any provision of this Subdivision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subsequent offer not made in reliance on any exemption under Subdivision (4)?
    `the subsequent offer is made in reliance on an exemption under subsection (1) or section 280` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the subsequent offer made in reliance on the exemption under section 272B(1) or section 280?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272B(5)(g) both persons are counted` MEANS
    IF `an offer is made to a person in reliance on the exemption under subsection (1) with a view to the securities being subsequently offered for sale to another person` AND (`the subsequent offer is not made in reliance on an exemption under any provision of this Subdivision` OR `the subsequent offer is made in reliance on an exemption under subsection (1) or section 280`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where — (i) an offer of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts is made to a person in reliance on the exemption under subsection (1) with a view to those securities"

@ref s 272B(5)(e) (src:43338-43340)
GIVEN
    `the offers are made by a person as an agent of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the offers made by a person as an agent of another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272B(5)(e) the offers are treated as made by that other person` MEANS
    IF `the offers are made by a person as an agent of another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph speaks only of offers made by an agent

DECLARE `s 272B(3) an earlier offeree` HAS
    `the day the earlier offer was made to the offeree` IS A DATE
    `the number of persons the earlier offer to the offeree counted as` IS A NUMBER
    `the earlier offer was made by the same person of securities issued by the same entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earlier offer was a closely related offer made by that person or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earlier offer was made in reliance on the exemption under section 272B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earlier offer was made in reliance on the exemption under section 302C` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:43283 | (3) In determining whether offers of securities or securities‑based
-- src:43284 | derivatives contracts by a person are made to no more than the
-- src:43285 | applicable number of persons specified in subsection (1)(a) within a
-- src:43286 | period of 12 months, the following persons must be included:
-- src:43288 | (a) each person to whom an offer of securities or
-- src:43289 | securities‑based derivatives contracts issued by the same
-- src:43290 | entity is made by the firstmentioned person within that
-- src:43291 | period in reliance on the exemption under this section;
-- src:43293 | (b) each person to whom an offer of securities or
-- src:43294 | securities‑based derivatives contracts of an entity or a
-- src:43295 | business trust, or units in a collective investment scheme, is
-- src:43296 | made by the firstmentioned person or another person
-- src:43297 | where such offer is a closely related offer, within that
-- src:43298 | period in reliance on the exemption under this section or
-- src:43299 | section 302C.
@ref s 272B(3) (src:43283-43299)
GIVEN
    `the first day of the period of 12 months asked about` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period of 12 months asked about?
    `the earlier offerees` IS A LIST OF `s 272B(3) an earlier offeree` @desc For each person to whom an earlier offer was made: the day, how many persons the offer counted as, whether it was made by the same person of securities issued by the same entity, whether it was a closely related offer, and whether it relied on the exemption under section 272B or section 302C. (An empty list: none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 272B(3) the number of persons to whom earlier offers were made that must be included` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier offerees`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN o FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF (o's `the day the earlier offer was made to the offeree` AT LEAST `the first day of the period of 12 months asked about`) AND (o's `the day the earlier offer was made to the offeree` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the first day of the period of 12 months asked about` 12 Months)) AND (((o's `the earlier offer was made by the same person of securities issued by the same entity`) AND (o's `the earlier offer was made in reliance on the exemption under section 272B`)) OR ((o's `the earlier offer was a closely related offer made by that person or another person`) AND ((o's `the earlier offer was made in reliance on the exemption under section 272B`) OR (o's `the earlier offer was made in reliance on the exemption under section 302C`))))
        THEN (o's `the number of persons the earlier offer to the offeree counted as`) PLUS (`s 272B(3) the number of persons to whom earlier offers were made that must be included` `the first day of the period of 12 months asked about` rest)
        ELSE `s 272B(3) the number of persons to whom earlier offers were made that must be included` `the first day of the period of 12 months asked about` rest
    -- FORK s272B-3 | s 272B(3) | `s 272B(3) the number of persons to whom earlier offers were made that must be included` | took (a) as an earlier offer by the first person of securities issued by the same entity in reliance on section 272B, and (b) as a closely related offer by that person or another in reliance on section 272B or section 302C, each within the period of 12 months beginning on the first day asked about | other reading none the text supports; the period is the caller's window, as in section 272A(1)(a) | licence the text's own words. The function adds numbers; it never answers JUST FALSE.

GIVEN
    `the number of persons this offer counts as, as section 272B(5) counts them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons do the offers made now count as, counted as section 272B(5) directs?
    `the number of persons to whom earlier offers were made that must be included, as section 272B(3) counts them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons to whom earlier offers were made must be included, as section 272B(3) directs?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 272B(3) the number of persons to whom offers are made within the period of 12 months` MEANS
    `the number of persons this offer counts as, as section 272B(5) counts them` PLUS `the number of persons to whom earlier offers were made that must be included, as section 272B(3) counts them`

-- src:43303 | (4) Whether an offer is a closely related offer under subsection (3)
-- src:43304 | is determined by considering such factors as the Authority may
-- src:43305 | prescribe.
@ref s 272B(4) (src:43303-43305)
GIVEN
    `the offer is a closely related offer on the factors the Authority has prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer, on considering the factors the Authority has prescribed, a closely related offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272B(4) the offer is a closely related offer` MEANS
    IF `the offer is a closely related offer on the factors the Authority has prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "is determined by considering such factors as the Authority may prescribe"

-- src:43222 | (a) the offers are made to no more than 50 persons within any
-- src:43223 | period of 12 months;
@ref s 272B(1)(a) (src:43222-43223)
GIVEN
    `the number of persons to whom the offers are made within the period of 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many persons are the offers made within the period of 12 months, counted as sections 272B(3) and (5) direct?
    `the applicable number of persons` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the applicable number of persons: 50, or the other number the Authority has prescribed under section 272B(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272B(1)(a) the offers are made to no more than the applicable number of persons within the period of 12 months` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons to whom the offers are made within the period of 12 months` AT MOST `the applicable number of persons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the offers are made to no more than 50 persons within any period of 12 months"

-- src:43225 | (b) none of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement
-- src:43226 | making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended
-- src:43227 | offer;
@ref s 272B(1)(b) (src:43225-43227)
GIVEN
    `one of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any of the offers accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer? ("Advertisement" has the meaning given by section 272A(10).)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272B(1)(b) none of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement` MEANS
    IF `one of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "none of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement making an offer or calling attention to the offer or intended offer"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:43379 | (6) In subsection (1)(b), “advertisement” has the meaning given by
-- src:43380 | section 272A(10).
@ref s 272B(6) (src:43379-43380)
GIVEN
    `the communication is a written or printed communication, a communication by radio, television or other medium of communication, or a communication by means of a recorded telephone message` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication a written or printed communication, a communication by radio, television or other medium of communication, or a communication by means of a recorded telephone message?
    `the communication is published in connection with an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication published in connection with an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `the communication is a document purporting to describe the securities or the business and affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the business trust, and purporting to have been prepared for delivery to and review by persons to whom the offer is made so as to assist them in making an investment decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication a document that purports to describe the securities or contracts being offered, or the business and affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the business trust, and purports to have been prepared for delivery to and review by the persons to whom the offer is made so as to assist them in making an investment decision?
    `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under this Act, or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication a publication that consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under the Securities and Futures Act 2001, or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange?
    `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting, or a presentation of material on matters so contained at the general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the communication a publication that consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting of the person making the offer, the issuer, the unitholders of the business trust, the underlying entity or any entity, or a presentation of oral or written material on matters so contained in the notice or report at the general meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272B(6) the communication is an advertisement for subsection (1)(b)` MEANS
    `s 272A(10) the communication is an advertisement` `the communication is a written or printed communication, a communication by radio, television or other medium of communication, or a communication by means of a recorded telephone message` `the communication is published in connection with an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` `the communication is a document purporting to describe the securities or the business and affairs of the person making the offer, the issuer, the underlying entity or the business trust, and purporting to have been prepared for delivery to and review by persons to whom the offer is made so as to assist them in making an investment decision` `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a disclosure, notice or report required under this Act, or any listing rules or other requirements of an approved exchange or overseas exchange` `the communication is a publication that consists solely of a notice or report of a general meeting or proposed general meeting, or a presentation of material on matters so contained at the general meeting`

-- src:43229 | (c) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred in
-- src:43230 | connection with each offer other than those incurred for
-- src:43231 | administrative or professional services, or by way of
-- src:43232 | commission or fee for services rendered by —
-- src:43234 | (i) the holder of a capital markets services licence to
-- src:43235 | deal in capital markets products that are securities or
-- src:43236 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:43238 | (ii) an exempt person in respect of dealing in capital
-- src:43239 | markets products that are securities or
-- src:43240 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:43242 | (iii) a person who is licensed, approved, authorised or
-- src:43243 | otherwise regulated under the laws, codes or other
-- src:43244 | requirements of any foreign jurisdiction in respect of
-- src:43245 | dealing in capital markets products that are securities
-- src:43246 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts; or
-- src:43248 | (iv) a person who is exempt from the laws, codes or
-- src:43249 | requirements mentioned in sub‑paragraph (iii) in
-- src:43250 | respect of dealing in capital markets products that are
-- src:43251 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:43252 | and
@ref s 272B(1)(c) (src:43229-43252)
GIVEN
    `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with each offer` IS A LIST OF `s 272A(1)(d) kind of selling or promotional expense` @desc What are the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with each offer? (An empty list: none are paid or incurred.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272B(1)(c) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred other than those the paragraph allows` MEANS
    `s 272A(1)(d) the selling or promotional expenses are ones the exemption allows` `the kinds of the selling or promotional expenses paid or incurred in connection with each offer`
    -- The kinds of s 272A(1)(d)(i) to (iii)(B) are the kinds of s 272B(1)(c)(i) to (iv): the same four commission-or-fee persons and the administrative or professional services.

-- src:43254 | (d) no prospectus in respect of any of the offers has been
-- src:43255 | registered by the Authority or, where a prospectus has been
-- src:43256 | registered —
-- src:43261 | (i) the prospectus has expired pursuant to section 250;
-- src:43262 | or
-- src:43264 | (ii) the person making the offer has before making the
-- src:43265 | offer —
-- src:43267 | (A) informed the Authority by written notice of its
-- src:43268 | intent to make the offer in reliance on the
-- src:43269 | exemption under this subsection; and
-- src:43271 | (B) taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the
-- src:43272 | person to whom the offer is made that the offer
-- src:43273 | is made in reliance on the exemption under this
-- src:43274 | subsection.
@ref s 272B(1)(d) (src:43254-43274)
GIVEN
    `a prospectus in respect of any of the offers has been registered by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority registered a prospectus in respect of any of the offers?
    `the prospectus has expired under section 250` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prospectus expired pursuant to section 250? (Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (2), another part's answer.)
    `the person making the offer has before making the offer informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer, before making the offer, informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under section 272B(1)?
    `the person making the offer has before making the offer taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the person to whom the offer is made that the offer is made in reliance on the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person making the offer, before making the offer, taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the person to whom the offer is made that the offer is made in reliance on the exemption under section 272B(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272B(1)(d) no prospectus is registered, or the registered prospectus has expired or the Authority and the offeree have been told` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a prospectus in respect of any of the offers has been registered by the Authority`) OR `the prospectus has expired under section 250` OR (`the person making the offer has before making the offer informed the Authority by written notice of its intent to make the offer in reliance on the exemption under this subsection` AND `the person making the offer has before making the offer taken reasonable steps to inform in writing the person to whom the offer is made that the offer is made in reliance on the exemption`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no prospectus in respect of any of the offers has been registered by the Authority or, where a prospectus has been registered"

-- src:43217 | 272B.—(1) Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other
-- src:43218 | than section 257) do not apply to offers of securities or
-- src:43219 | securities‑based derivatives contracts of an entity or of a business
-- src:43220 | trust that are made by a person if —
@ref s 272B(1) (src:43217-43220)
GIVEN
    `paragraph (a), the number of persons` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272B(1)(a) the offers are made to no more than the applicable number of persons within the period of 12 months` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (b), no advertisement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272B(1)(b) none of the offers is accompanied by an advertisement` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (c), the selling or promotional expenses` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272B(1)(c) no selling or promotional expenses are paid or incurred other than those the paragraph allows` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `paragraph (d), the prospectus` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 272B(1)(d) no prospectus is registered, or the registered prospectus has expired or the Authority and the offeree have been told` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272B(1) the offers are exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`paragraph (a), the number of persons` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (b), no advertisement` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (c), the selling or promotional expenses` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`paragraph (d), the prospectus` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to offers of securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of an entity or of a business trust that are made by a person if"
        IF (`paragraph (a), the number of persons` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (b), no advertisement` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (c), the selling or promotional expenses` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`paragraph (d), the prospectus` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a paragraph is not answered
    -- FORK s272B-1 | s 272B(1) | `s 272B(1) the offers are exempt from Subdivisions (1A), (2) and (3) of this Division (other than section 257)` | took JUST FALSE where a paragraph (a) to (d) fails (conditions of an "if") | other reading NOTHING ("if A then B" does not say "if not A then not B") | licence {IN-SHORT}; under "Marginal readings for a lawyer"
